        <p>Can cleaning itself help? One small study suggests it might. Florida State University researchers asked 51 students to wash dishes, some after a short instruction to pay mindful attention (<a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s12671-014-0360-9" rel="noopener">Hanley et al., 2015</a>). According to the <a href="https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2015/10/151001165852.htm" rel="noopener">university's summary</a>, mindful dish washers reported a 27% decrease in nervousness and a 25% increase in feeling inspired; the comparison group did not. With a small student sample, this is promising rather than conclusive.</p>

